\label{l23}
Suppose that $M N H L=v$, and $M$, $N$ and $H$ satisfy one of the following $3$ conditions:

(1). $M \ll v^{\frac{18}{35}},\ N \gg H,\ N^{\frac{3}{4}}H \ll v^{\frac{9}{35}},\ N H^{\frac{1}{2}} \ll v^{\frac{9}{35}},\ N^{\frac{7}{4}} H^{\frac{3}{2}} \ll v^{\frac{18}{35}}$;

(2). $M \ll v^{\frac{18}{35}},\ N \ll v^{\frac{9}{35}},\ H \ll v^{\frac{9}{140}}$;

(3). $M \ll v^{\frac{18}{35}},\ N^2 H \ll v^{\frac{18}{35}},\ H \ll v^{\frac{9}{70}}$.

Then for $\sqrt{L} \leqslant T \leqslant x^{\frac{1}{2}-\frac{\varepsilon}{6}}$, we have
$$
\int_{T}^{2 T}|M(b+i t) N(b+i t) H(b+i t) L(b+i t) P^K (b+i t)| d t \ll (\log x)^{-B}.
$$
